- › Logistics employee 
 €16.49 Den Bosch ⏰ 36-40 uur Fulltime Logistiek 
 Over de functie 
Join My Jewellery as a Logistics Employee in Den Bosch! ✨ 
Do you have logistics experience and are you looking for a new challenge? My Jewellery is looking for a full-time Logistics Employee to join our distribution center in Den Bosch. 
You'll work 40 hours per week in a fixed two-shift rotation, alternating weekly between: - 06:00 AM - 03:00 PM - 03:00 PM - 12:00 AM 
Together with your team, you'll make sure customer orders are picked, processed, and prepared for shipment accurately and on time. 
 Jouw nieuwe werkplek 
As an Order Picker, you are an essential part of the logistics team. You make sure customer orders are picked correctly and ready for shipment. With a handheld scanner and order cart, you'll navigate the warehouse and collect the required products. Your accuracy and eye for detail help ensure every order is complete and delivered on time. 
Pick and collect orders using a handheld scanner 
Transport picked products to the packing department 
Check orders for accuracy, completeness, and quality 
Support the team with processing returned items 
 Dit bieden wij jou 
✅ An attractive hourly wage of €16.49 , including shift allowance (approximately €2,860 gross per month based on 40 hours); 
✅ A clear and fixed work schedule; 
✅ A modern warehouse with a great working atmosphere; 
✅ A young and enthusiastic team; 
✅ Career growth opportunities, for example towards Operator or Inventory Controller positions; 
✅ The opportunity to obtain a Forklift or Reach Truck Certificate; 
✅ Travel allowance and free safety shoes through Westerduin; 
✅ Holiday pay, paid vacation days, and pension accrual; 
✅ Healthy meals available through the AH to go vending machine. 
 Dit vragen wij van jou 
✔ Available to start immediately; 
✔ At least 2 years of logistics experience; 
✔ Good command of Dutch or English. 
Romy de Laat 
Recruiter 
Hoe kan ik je...

Would you like to contribute to flawless mail delivery and are you looking for a flexible part-time job? Become a mail preparer at our client in Assen! In this role, you will be responsible for ensuring that mail is correctly sorted and prepared for dispatch.

As a mail preparer in Assen, you are responsible for accurately sorting incoming mail. You will check addresses and shipping details and use various mail processing machines to handle the mail efficiently. The job requires precision and good physical condition, as you will be working primarily on your feet. You should also be open to working overtime to assist your colleagues during backlogs or busy periods.

What we ask for:

- No minimum educational requirements;
- Precision and attention to detail;
- Enthusiastic and motivated attitude;
- You speak either Dutch or English;

As a C Driver, you are responsible for driving the truck and delivering a wide range of food and non-food products to customers such as restaurants, cafés, sports clubs, and company canteens. Together with your driver’s assistant, you handle loading and unloading and ensure deliveries are completed safely and efficiently.

This is an active role where you are frequently on the move and work in all weather conditions. You will primarily work from Monday to Friday, with regular shifts on Saturdays. Your start time is fixed, but flexibility is required regarding your finishing time.

At the start of the day, you review the route together, load the truck, and begin your deliveries. You also handle basic administrative tasks and provide friendly, customer-focused service. After completing your route, you return to the depot and check in for any additional assignments.

If you perform well, you will have the opportunity to obtain your CE license and grow within the company.

- Valid Category C driving licence and Code 95;
- In possession of a digital driver card;
- Own transport (car/moped/scooter/motorcycle);
- Experience as a driver;
- Living in the vicinity of Berkel en Rodenrijs;
- Presentable appearance;
- Available full-time and flexible;
- Good command of the English language, both spoken and written;

From the job description, you may have already noticed that this is a physically demanding role in which you do more than just drive the vehicle. It is therefore important that this suits you. If so, we encourage you to apply. Who knows, you might soon start working for our client.
